= Strikes and factory councils

The party's strength lies in the workplace, in the factory councils and the strike committees, and not in the meeting hall. The free trade unions are run by Social Democrats who distrust us, and the workers are often more militant than their officials.

- @councils: Organise a strike through the factory councils.
- @opposition: Build a communist opposition inside the free unions.
- @fractions: Put Walcher's union fractions behind the strike committees.
- @root: Not this month.
- @easy_discard

@fractions
view-if: walcher_advisor = 1
subtitle: Walcher is in the leadership. · dev: y23_unity +1, y23_strikes +1, workers_kpd +3×m, kf_right_strength +1
on-arrival: y23_unity += 1; y23_strikes += 1; workers_kpd += 3*campaign_mult; kf_right_strength += 1
go-to: root

Walcher's union men, who know every works committee in the Ruhr and in Stuttgart, bring the strike committees and the union locals to the same table. The strike is solid, and the SPD locals notice who made it so.

@councils
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, y23_strikes +1, workers_kpd +3×m, workers_spd −1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; y23_strikes += 1; workers_kpd += 3*campaign_mult; workers_spd -= 1
go-to: root

The councils call the workers out over wages and hours. The strike is solid in some plants and a failure in others, and the union leaders, who did not call it, spend the week denouncing it. The workers do not forget who walked out with them.

@opposition
subtitle: No cost. · dev: y23_unity +1, workers_kpd +2×m, kf_left_dissent +2
on-arrival: y23_unity += 1; workers_kpd += 2*campaign_mult; kf_left_dissent += 2
go-to: root

Our members join the union locals, speak at every meeting and stand for every post. The officials answer with expulsions, which turns our members into martyrs and, at the same time, makes it harder for us to reach the ones who stay. Slow work, and not the work the Left wants.
